  <!--
    Every word the settings page shows. Home Assistant translates an integration's own surfaces and an add-on's
    configuration options, and translates nothing at all inside a page an add-on serves, so the page carries its
    own words and picks its own language from what the browser asks for.

    A second language is a file beside this one, named for its culture, with no change to any component.
    en-GB at the source: colour, behaviour, initialise. An American spelling is a defect wherever it appears.
    Every label and every status is a few words. What needs explaining goes in a Help entry, behind an icon.
    Whole words only: no abbreviation, and no text left for a container to clip. A label that does not fit
    gets a shorter whole word.
  -->
